What it does not cover

When it runs, the sample loads Drop Cowboy Building Blocks (The Dock, the
contact card, the pipeline board, the shared inbox, the campaign hub, the
phone hub and others) from https://webforms.dropcowboy.com, and it calls Drop
Cowboy APIs and services. Those scripts, APIs and services are proprietary to
Drop Cowboy. They are not part of this sample, they are not licensed under MIT,
and your use of them is governed by the Drop Cowboy Terms of Service:
https://www.dropcowboy.com/terms

No Drop Cowboy source code is included in this folder. The sample refers to
Building Blocks only by URL and loads them in the browser at runtime.

Third-party packages

The sample's package.json, requirements.txt and requirements-dev.txt files
list open-source dependencies (for example Express, React, Flask). They are
installed from their public registries under their own licenses and are not
included in this folder.
